## SQ-SMK-51 | Storage Delight boots: jar found, no error naming it
@group A
@commands Boot; grep `logs/debug.log` for the jar; grep `logs/latest.log` for errors
@pass jar found with `{storagedelight}`; no dependency error; no ERROR line naming `storagedelight`
@fails Jar missing, the upstream `storagedelight-*.jar` loaded beside it, a replaced registry class broken
bootexpect Done \(
bootreject (?i)storagedelight.*(missing|requires)
bootreject /ERROR\].*\bstoragedelight\b
bootreject DuplicateModsFound|Found duplicate mods
shell grep -q "Found valid mod file repackedStorage-[^ ]*\.jar with .storagedelight." logs/debug.log

## SQ-SMK-52 | Storage Delight items and recipes, added sets included
@group A
@commands `/cdevtest reg item ^storagedelight: max=1`; `/cdevtest recipes storagedelight: max=1`; `/cdevtest makes storagedelight:acacia_drawer`; `/cdevtest reg block ^storagedelight:bamboo_drawer$`
@pass 130 or more items (140 on 2026-11-15); 130 or more recipes (140); a recipe makes the acacia drawer; the added bamboo drawer is registered
@fails The repack's replaced `BlockRegistry` / `ItemRegistry` dropping entries, overlay recipes missing
> cdevtest reg item ^storagedelight: max=1
> cdevtest recipes storagedelight: max=1
> cdevtest makes storagedelight:acacia_drawer
> cdevtest reg block ^storagedelight:bamboo_drawer$
